+/* $Id$ */
+/** @file
+ * DrvLinuxBridge - Linux TAP network transport driver with host bridge attachment.
+ *
+ * This driver connects a virtual NIC to a Linux host bridge (e.g. "vboxbr0")
+ * without requiring any VirtualBox kernel modules:
+ *
+ *      1. It opens /dev/net/tun and creates a TAP interface named "vboxtapX"
+ *         (IFF_TAP|IFF_NO_PI, non-persistent, so it vanishes when the VM
+ *         releases the fd).  Creating a new interface requires
+ *         CAP_NET_ADMIN, so when TUNSETIFF fails with EPERM the driver
+ *         asks the setuid helper to create a persistent interface owned
+ *         by the VM user first and then attaches to it by name.
+ *      2. It invokes the setuid-root helper "VBoxNetBrCtl" to enslave the TAP
+ *         interface to the configured host bridge and bring it up.  The
+ *         helper is restricted to "vboxtap*" names and talks rtnetlink
+ *         directly, so no external tools are involved.
+ *
+ * The driver is attached via the generic network attachment:
+ *      VBoxManage modifyvm <vm> --nic<N> generic --driver<N> LinuxBridge \
+ *          --property<N> bridge=vboxbr0
+ *
+ * The frame pump is modeled on DrvTAP.cpp.
+ */
+
